  "Scarcity": {"Explanation": "The email creates a sense of urgency by stating that proposals need to be sent by September 30, 1997, limiting the time available."},
  "Authority": {"Explanation": "The email claims credibility through the involvement of recognized institutions (University of Sheffield, University of Leeds, Leeds Studies in English) and the participation of well-known scholars (Bill Kretzschmar, Jim Milroy), establishing authority in the field."},
  "Commitment/Consistency": {"Explanation": "The email references prior behavior (the conference has been held previously) to build on the existing momentum and encourage further action."},
  "Liking": {"Explanation": "The email uses personalization by mentioning specific scholars (Bill Kretzschmar, Jim Milroy) and inviting the recipient to contribute to the conference, building a sense of rapport and familiarity."},
  "Social proof": {"Explanation": "The email mentions the involvement of well-known scholars and the participation of people from different English-using world, creating a sense of social proof and credibility."}}
}

